// =============================================================================
// Chora Closure Orchestrator Service (gRPC)
// =============================================================================
//
// Source-of-truth: docs/architecture-review-inputs-2026-05-07.md Tier 3 D11
//   + .claude/rules/ddd-enforcement.md ("Account Closure (federated saga)")
//   + .claude/skills/account-closure-saga/SKILL.md
//
// Federated PII closure saga coordinator. NEVER hard-deletes — pseudonymises
// + crypto-shreds. Preserves FK integrity + audit trail + GDPR Art. 17.
//
// 5-state machine (per ddd-enforcement):
//   ACTIVE → CLOSING (grace) → SUSPENDED → PSEUDONYMIZED →
//          COLD_ARCHIVED → CRYPTO_SHREDDED
//
// Saga state lives in chora_identity (Platform-owned). Per-domain
// pseudonymisation is triggered via Pub/Sub events (each domain owns its
// PII_Closure_Map.yaml declaring fields-to-tokenize, retention rules,
// on-creator-closure behaviour).
//
// CMEK per-tenant master key + per-user DEK; deleting DEK = crypto-shred
// (data unrecoverable).
//
// This service exposes the synchronous control plane (start saga, query
// state, fan-out triggers). The actual per-domain work runs asynchronously
// via Pub/Sub events emitted by this service.
//
// Deployed in chora-489812 team-platform; Team 3 (Platform) owned.
// mTLS via Cloud Service Mesh; SPIFFE identity in mesh.
// =============================================================================

